cpufreq: demote "Running at unlisted initial frequency" message to debug

On ipq53xx U-Boot hands the CPU over parked on GPLL0 (the Stromer Plus APSS
PLL cannot be reconfigured while it drives the CPU, so it is parked on GPLL0
and switched back afterwards).  clk_get_rate() therefore reports 799999999 Hz
=> 799999 kHz, which is not present in the speed-bin filtered OPP table, so
cpufreq_online() prints:

  cpufreq: cpufreq_online: CPU0: Running at unlisted initial frequency:
  799999 KHz, changing to: 1100000 KHz

The frequency is still corrected as intended (to the lowest listed OPP), only
the log line is noise.  Print it at debug level so the boot log stays clean;
no functional change.  It can still be seen with dynamic debug enabled.

--- a/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq.c
@@ -1532,7 +1532,7 @@
 			 * frequency for longer duration. Hence, a BUG_ON().
 			 */
 			BUG_ON(ret);
-			pr_info("%s: CPU%d: Running at unlisted initial frequency: %u KHz, changing to: %u KHz\n",
+			pr_debug("%s: CPU%d: Running at unlisted initial frequency: %u KHz, changing to: %u KHz\n",
 				__func__, policy->cpu, old_freq, policy->cur);
 		}
 	}
